204 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 183 0 R
/T (In Idealclockland, clocks work ideally. When one looks at the clock, they will see two hands: the hour hand and the minute hand. In idealclockland, clocks are designed better than normal analog clocks we use. The clock is divided to 60 equal arcs like ours, but the hands differ in the way they work. At the start of every minute, the minute hand progresses to the next segment instantly. \(It "teleports" so to speak\). Likewise, at the start of every hour, the hour hand progresses to the arc located five segments further. The example image explains the process.)
/E (In Idealclockland, clocks work ideally. When one looks at the clock, they will see two hands: the hour hand and the minute hand. In idealclockland, clocks are designed better than normal analog clocks we use. The clock is divided to 60 equal arcs like ours, but the hands differ in the way they work. At the start of every minute, the minute hand progresses to the next segment instantly. \(It "teleports" so to speak\). Likewise, at the start of every hour, the hour hand progresses to the arc located five segments further. The example image explains the process.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
